hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1861","Narrated Isma'il bin Abi Khalid: From his father that Abu Hurairah informed them that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"When the servant of one of you has endured heat and smoke preparing his food for him"
"1862","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Spread the (greetings of) Salam"
"1863","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"(All of you) worship Ar-Rahman"
"1864","Narrated Anas bin Malik: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Take the 'Asha' meal"
"1865","Narrated 'Umar bin Abi Salamah: That he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he has some food. He said: \"Sit down O my son! Mention Allah's Name and eat with your right hand"
"1866","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Qutaybah Abū Rajā' narrated to us, Jarīr narrated to us, from 'Aṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib, from Sa'īd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both), that the Prophet ﷺ said:**\n\n> *\"Indeed, blessing descends in the middle of the food. Therefore, eat from its edges and do not eat from its centre.\"*\n\nAbū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **\"This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. It is known only from the narration of 'Aṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib. Shu'bah and al-Thawrī both narrated it from 'Aṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib. In this chapter, there is also a narration from Ibn 'Umar (may Allāh be pleased with him).\"**\n\n---\n\n### Scholarly Notes:\n\n- **Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ**: Al-Tirmidhī graded this narration as both *ḥasan* (good) and *ṣaḥīḥ* (authentic), indicating its strong chain of transmission.\n- **Ibn 'Abbās** (may Allāh be pleased with him): The cousin of the Prophet ﷺ and a renowned exegete (*mufassir*) of the Qur'ān.\n- **Sa'īd ibn Jubayr**: A distinguished Successor (*tābi'ī*) and one of the most eminent students of Ibn 'Abbās.\n- **'Aṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib**: A well-known narrator from Kufa, whose transmissions were preserved by major compilers.\n- The hadith teaches **etiquette of eating** (*ādāb al-akl*), instructing Muslims to eat from the sides of the food so that the **barakah** (divine blessing) may remain and descend upon the meal."
"1867","then let him say: 'Bismillah.' If he forgets in the beginning, then let him say: 'Bismillah Fi Awwalihi Wa Akhirih (In the Name of Allah in its beginning and its end.) \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1858 Arabic Hadees: 1858\""
"1868","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Indeed Ash-Shaitan has a sense of taste"
"1869","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever spends the night with [a smell] on his hand and something happens to him"
"1870","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Every intoxicant is Khamr"
"1871","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever drinks Khamr"
"1872","Narrated 'Aishah: That the Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about Bit' so he said: \"All drinks that intoxicate are unlawful.\" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1873","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Prophet (ﷺ) \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\" He said: There are narrations on this topic from 'Umar"
"1874","Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whatever a lot of it intoxicates"
"1875","Narrated 'Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful. Whatever a Faraq of it intoxicates"
"1876","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar al-Baghdadi and Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who both said: narrated to us Yahya ibn Hassān, narrated to us Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Hishām ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ā’ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: “A house in which there are no dates, its inhabitants are hungry.”\n\nHe (the compiler) said: In this chapter, there is also a narration from Salmā, the wife of Abū Rāfi’.\n\nAbū Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a hasan gharīb hadith; we do not know it from the hadith of Hishām ibn Urwah except through this chain. He added: I asked al-Bukhārī about this hadith, and he said: “I do not know anyone who narrated it other than Yahya ibn Hassān.”"
"1877","Narrated Zadhan: \"I asked Ibn 'Umar about what containers the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited. He informed us in your language"
"1878","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Jābir ibn 'Abdullāh** (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) took the hand of a person afflicted with leprosy, placed him alongside him in the dish, and then said:\n\n**\"Eat: In the name of Allāh, placing trust in Allāh and relying upon Him.\"**\n\n---\n\n**Abū 'Īsā** (Imam al-Tirmidhī) commented: This is a *gharīb* (uncommon/singular) hadith. We know it only through the narration of Yūnus ibn Muḥammad from al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah. He further clarified that al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah referred to here is a Basran shaykh, and that there is another al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah who is an Egyptian shaykh, more reliable and more well-known than this one. He also noted that Shu'bah narrated a similar hadith from Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd from Ibn Buraydah, that Ibn 'Umar (may Allāh be pleased with him) took the hand of a leper, and that the hadith of Shu'bah is, in his view, more established and more authentic."
"1879","Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited using (certain) containers. So the Ansar complained about that to him. They said: 'We will have no vessels!' so he said: 'If so then use them.'\" He said: There are narrations on this topic from Ibn Mas'ud"
"1880","Narrated 'Aishah: \"We would prepare Nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in a water-skin which was fastened at the top and it has a small hole. We would prepare Nabidh in it during the morning"
"1881","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Indeed Khamr comes from wheat"
"1882","Narrated 'Umar: \"Indeed Khamr comes from wheat.\" And he mentioned this Hadith"
"1883","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: \"Indeed Khamr comes from wheat.\" [After mentioning this"
"1884","Narrated Abu Kathir As-Suhaimi: That he heard Abu Hurairah saying that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Khamr comes from these two trees (plants): The datepalm and the grape (vine).\" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Abu Kathir As-Suhaimi is Al-Ghubari"
"1885","Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited making Nabidh from unripend dates and fresh dates together. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1886","Narrated Abu Sa'eed: \"The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited mixing of unripe dates and dates"
"1887","Narrated Shu'bah bin Al-Hakam: \"I heard Ibn Abi Laila narrating that Hudhaifah asked for water"
"1888","Narrated Qatadah: From Anas: \"The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited that a man should drink while standing.\" (Qatadah said:) So it was said: \"And eating ?\" He (Anas) said: \"That is worse.\" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1889","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \"We would eat during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while we were walking"
"1890","Narrated Al-Jarud bin Al-'Ala': \"The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited drinking while standing.\" And there are narrations on this topic from Abu Sa'eed"
"1891","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: \"The Prophet (ﷺ) drank from Zamzam while he was standing.\" He said: There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"
"1892","Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani, who narrated from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, who said: Ibn Jurayj informed us that Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed him that 'Ata' ibn Yasar informed him that Umm Salamah"
"1893","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Let none of you drink all at once like the camel. But drink two or three times"
"1894","Salamah ibn Shabib, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, and Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawri narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \"The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to love sweets and honey.\" This is a hasan sahih gharib hadith. It was also narrated by Ali ibn Muhsin from Hisham ibn Urwah, and the hadith contains more words than this."
"1895","Narrated Abu Sa’id Al Khudri : That the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited blowing into the drink. A man said: \"What about if one sees something floating in the vessel?\" He said: \"Spill it out (removing that).\" He said: \"I can not drink in one breath.\" He said: \"Then remove the cup away from your mouth.\" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1896","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited breathing in the vessel"
